They've started to make a creeping appearance in recent versions.
"You caitiff!", "You feel like a glutton!" for knights.
"You feel guilty," "Your armour is rather cumbersome..." (okay, so
there were no Monks before these messages, but it's the same sort of
thing IMO.)

These messages aren't necessarily bad things, but it does seem to show
a trend towards giving the player information about obscure game
mechanical goings-on, which never really used to happen.

(Fair enough, I don't know how, short of reading spoilers, players
ever used to know that knights had to be chivalrous.)

> Yes, I do think that axes doing extra damage to wood golems is obvious,
> just as fire brand doing extra damage to watery creatures is.

I didn't even know about either of those. But it was a lot nicer to
find out this way, after having been playing the game for years, than
to have been told by a message the first time it came up. The latter
would almost be showing off.
